      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For a standard single-family home in Utah, the average cost for a full roof replacement ranges from $8,500 to $18,000 for traditional asphalt shingles. Most homeowners with a typical 2,000-square-foot home map out a total cost of around $11,000 to $14,800 .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "$8,500 to $18,000"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The overall cost depends heavily on your home's total square footage, the material you select, and specific local requirements (like ice and water shielding for heavy Utah snows)."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Breakdown by Home Size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Utah roofing contractors typically quote a rate of $4.00 to $8.25 per square foot for labor and asphalt materials combined."
      },
