      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Breakdown by Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Material tier impacts the total invoice drastically. Given Utah\u2019s intense UV exposure and heavy winter snow loads, upgraded options like metal or premium architectural shingles are popular for longevity."
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Architectural Shingles: $8,500 \u2013 $18,000 total ($4.00 \u2013 $8.25/sq. ft.). This is the most common residential option across the Wasatch Front."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Premium Architectural (e.g., GAF Timberline UHDZ): $12,000 \u2013 $25,000 total. Thick, heavy-duty shingles featuring enhanced wind and algae warranties."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing (Standing Seam): $15,000 \u2013 $35,000 total ($8.00 \u2013 $17.00/sq. ft.). Highly durable, sheds heavy snow efficiently, and lasts 40\u201370 years."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flat Roof (TPO / Membrane): $6,000 \u2013 $22,500 total ($4.00 \u2013 $10.00/sq. ft.). Commonly utilized for modern homes or commercial spaces in Salt Lake City."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Utah-Specific Cost Factors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Ice and Water Shielding: Utah building codes require self-adhering ice and water barriers applied at the eaves to protect against ice damming. This adds roughly $300 to $500 to the contract."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Location Adjustments: Labor rates fluctuate by county. Salt Lake County roof replacements average slightly higher ($9,000 \u2013 $20,000) due to higher operational overhead, while Cache County and Weber County lean closer to $8,500 \u2013 $18,000 ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Plywood Decking Replacement: If the crew tears off your old shingles and finds rotted roof decking underneath, expect to pay $60 to $80 per sheet of new OSB plywood."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-Off Layers: Legally, a home can only hold up to two layers of shingles. If a contractor has to strip multiple layers of old roofing down to the wood, expect an extra $1,000 to $2,500 in labor and dumpster disposal fees."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you are looking to get precise estimates, I can help you figure out exactly what you need. Could you tell me:"
      },
